{%- comment -%}
  Search, as a plain GET form.

  Predictive search is switched on in this store's settings but had no entry
  point anywhere in the navigation — the rail and the menu sheet both dropped
  it, and so did the Explore overlay before them. With the launch collection
  landing in November that is a shop you cannot search.

  No JavaScript: it is a form pointed at Shopify's own search route, so it
  works with scripts off and needs nothing re-initialised when the theme editor
  re-renders the header.

  Accepts:
    variant - 'sheet' (mobile menu) or 'rail' (desktop)
    id      - unique suffix, since this renders in two places on one page
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign s_variant = variant | default: 'sheet' -%}

<form class="alp-search alp-search--{{ s_variant }}" action="{{ routes.search_url }}" method="get" role="search">
  <label class="visually-hidden" for="alp-search-{{ id }}">Search</label>
  <input
    class="alp-search__field"
    id="alp-search-{{ id }}"
    type="search"
    name="q"
    value="{{ search.terms | escape }}"
    placeholder="Search the shop"
    autocomplete="off"
  >
  <input type="hidden" name="options[prefix]" value="last">
  <button class="alp-search__go" type="submit" aria-label="Search">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true">
      <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"/><path d="M20 20l-3.5-3.5"/>
    </svg>
  </button>
</form>
